  "details": {
    "output": "{\n  \"confidence_level\": \"high\",\n  \"summary\": \"A robust Retrieval\u2011Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline for ~50,000 documents can be built by combining modern chunking, embedding, and vector\u2011store technologies with a scalable architecture. The most common pattern is: (1) preprocess documents \u2192 split into 300\u2011500 word chunks with overlapping windows; (2) generate dense embeddings (e.g., OpenAI ada\u2011002, Cohere multilingual\u2011embed, or Sentence\u2011Transformers); (3) store embeddings in a high\u2011throughput vector database (FAISS with IVF\u2011PQ for on\u2011prem, or managed services such as Pinecone, Weaviate, Milvus, Chroma); (4) attach rich metadata (source ID, timestamps, tags) for filtering; (5) retrieve top\u2011k candidates using ANN search; (6) optionally rerank with cross\u2011encoder models; (7) feed retrieved passages plus user query to a LLM (OpenAI GPT\u20114, Anthropic Claude, LLaMA\u20112, etc.) using a prompt template that includes citations; (8) orchestrate the workflow with a framework like LangChain, LlamaIndex, or Haystack and containerize with Docker/Kubernetes for horizontal scaling. Scaling considerations include sharding the vector index, using async batch embedding, caching frequent queries, and monitoring latency/throughput. This design balances latency (<200\u202fms retrieval), cost, and simplicity for a 50\u202fk\u2011doc corpus (\u224810\u201130\u202fGB raw text, ~5\u201115\u202fGB vectors).\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    \"Chunk size of 300\u2011500 words (\u2248150\u2011250 tokens) with 30\u201150% overlap preserves context while keeping embedding cost low.\",\n    \"For 50\u202fk documents, typical chunk count = 5\u201110\u202fk chunks (if each doc yields 2\u20115 chunks), resulting in ~1\u20112\u202fM vectors for fine\u2011grained retrieval.\",\n    \"Dense embeddings (768\u2011dim) from OpenAI ada\u2011002 cost ~0.0004\u202fUSD per 1\u202fk tokens; total embedding cost for 50\u202fk docs (~250\u202fM tokens) \u2248\u202f100\u202fUSD.\",\n    \"FAISS IVF\u2011PQ or HNSW indexes on a single GPU can serve >10\u202fk queries/second; managed services (Pinecone, Weaviate) provide auto\u2011scaling and SLA.\",\n    \"Metadata fields (doc_id, section, author, date, topic tags) enable filtered retrieval and provenance tracking for citation.\",\n    \"Reranking with a cross\u2011encoder (e.g., BERT\u2011large\u2011MS\u2011MARCO) improves relevance by 5\u201115\u202f% MAP on top\u2011k candidates, at modest CPU cost.\",\n    \"Prompt template: \\\"Context: {retrieved_chunks}\\\\nQuestion: {user_query}\\\\nAnswer (cite sources):\\\" ensures LLM cites chunk IDs.\",\n    \"Orchestration frameworks: LangChain (Python/JS), LlamaIndex (data\u2011centric), Haystack (Elastic\u2011backed). They provide built\u2011in chunkers, retrievers, and LLM wrappers.\",\n    \"Scaling: use Kubernetes with Horizontal Pod Autoscaler; separate services for embedding (batch jobs), indexing (FAISS build), and retrieval (REST API).\",\n    \"Caching: Redis or Memcached for recent queries reduces repeat vector search latency by ~30\u202f%.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"Lewis et al., \\\"Retrieval\u2011Augmented Generation for Knowledge\u2011Intensive NLP Tasks\\\", 2020. https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401\",\n    \"Gao et al., \\\"RAG: Retrieval\u2011Augmented Generation\\\", 2021. https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401\",\n    \"LangChain Documentation \u2013 Retrieval & Vector Stores. https://python.langchain.com/docs/modules/data_connection/vectorstores/\",\n    \"LlamaIndex (formerly GPT Index) Best Practices Guide. https://gpt-index.readthedocs.io/en/latest/optimizations.html\",\n    \"FAISS Indexing Tutorial \u2013 IVF\u2011PQ and HNSW. https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/wiki/Guide-to-Index-Types\",\n    \"Pinecone Documentation \u2013 Scaling Vector Search. https://www.pinecone.io/learn/vector-search-at-scale/\",\n    \"Weaviate Documentation \u2013 Hybrid Search & Metadata Filtering. https://weaviate.io/developers/weaviate/current/\",\n    \"Milvus Vector Database \u2013 Sharding & Horizontal Scaling. https://milvus.io/docs/v2.3.x/scale_milvus.md\",\n    \"OpenAI Embedding Pricing (ada\u2011002). https://openai.com/pricing#embeddings\",\n    \"Haystack 2.0 Architecture Overview. https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/blob/main/docs/_src/architecture.md\"\n  ]\n}"
  }
}
