  "details": {
    "output": "**Quantitative Analysis & Recommendations for a Retrieval\u2011Augmented Generation (RAG) Pipeline that will serve\u202f\u2248\u202f50\u202f000 documents**  \n\n---\n\n## 1.  Baseline Assumptions (derived from industry benchmarks and the limited artefacts in the repo)\n\n| Item | Assumption | Rationale |\n|------|------------|-----------|\n| **Average raw document size** | **2\u202fKB** (\u2248\u202f350\u202ftokens) | Typical knowledge\u2011base article, FAQ, or short report. |\n| **Document tokenisation** | **\u2248\u202f350\u202ftokens** per doc | 2\u202fKB \u2248\u202f350\u202ftokens with GPT\u20114 tokenizer. |\n| **Embedding model** | **OpenAI `text\u2011embedding\u2011ada\u2011002`** (1536\u2011dim float32) | Cheapest, high\u2011quality, widely\u2011used for RAG. |\n| **Embedding vector size** | **6\u202fKB** (1536\u202f\u00d7\u202f4\u202fbytes) | Float\u201132 representation. |\n| **Metadata per doc** | **\u2248\u202f200\u202fbytes** (id, title, source, timestamps) | Minimal indexing info. |\n| **Vector store** | **FAISS\u2011IVF\u2011PQ** (on\u2011prem) or **Pinecone** (managed) | Both support million\u2011scale vectors with sub\u2011ms latency. |\n| **Query model** | **GPT\u20114o** (or GPT\u20114\u2011Turbo) for generation | Current best\u2011in\u2011class LLM for answer synthesis. |\n| **Embedding API cost** | **$0.0004 /\u202f1\u202f000\u202ftokens** (Ada\u2011002) | Public pricing (Oct\u202f2024). |\n| **Generation API cost** | **$0.005\u202f/\u202f1\u202fk\u202ftokens** (GPT\u20114o) | Public pricing (Oct\u202f2024). |\n| **Compute for self\u2011hosted embeddings** | **NVIDIA A100 (40\u202fGB)** \u2013 2\u202f500\u202fembeddings\u202f/\u202fs (\u2248\u202f1\u202fM\u202ftokens\u202f/\u202fs) | Benchmarks from the OpenAI paper and community reports. |\n| **Concurrency target** | **10\u201120 simultaneous queries** | Typical SaaS load for a small\u2011to\u2011medium internal knowledge base. |\n\n---\n\n## 2.  Storage Requirements  \n\n| Component | Calculation | Size |\n|-----------|-------------|------|\n| **Raw documents** | 50\u202f000\u202f\u00d7\u202f2\u202fKB | **\u2248\u202f100\u202fMB** |\n| **Embedding vectors** | 50\u202f000\u202f\u00d7\u202f6\u202fKB | **\u2248\u202f300\u202fMB** |\n| **Metadata** | 50\u202f000\u202f\u00d7\u202f0.2\u202fKB | **\u2248\u202f10\u202fMB** |\n| **FAISS index overhead** (IVF\u2011PQ, 1\u202f%\u20112\u202f% overhead) | \u2248\u202f6\u202fMB | **\u2248\u202f6\u202fMB** |\n| **Total on\u2011disk** | 100\u202fMB\u202f+\u202f300\u202fMB\u202f+\u202f10\u202fMB\u202f+\u202f6\u202fMB | **\u2248\u202f416\u202fMB** |\n\n> **Take\u2011away:** Even a modest VM (e.g., 2\u202fvCPU, 8\u202fGB RAM, 1\u202fTB SSD) can comfortably host the entire vector store with plenty of headroom for future growth (10\u202f\u00d7\u202fsize \u2192 4\u202fGB).  \n\n---\n\n## 3.  Throughput & Latency  \n\n| Operation | Expected throughput (single node) | Latency (p99) | Notes |\n|-----------|-----------------------------------|---------------|-------|\n| **Embedding (batch)** | 2\u202f500\u202fembeddings\u202f/\u202fs (\u2248\u202f8\u202f800\u202ftokens\u202f/\u202fs) \u2192 **\u2248\u202f180\u202fKB\u202f/\u202fs** | 30\u202fms per batch (64\u202fdocs) | Using `text\u2011embedding\u2011ada\u2011002` via API; batch size 64 gives best cost\u2011per\u2011token efficiency. |\n| **Full dataset embedding** | 50\u202f000\u202f/\u202f2\u202f500\u202f\u2248\u202f20\u202fs (plus API overhead) \u2192 **\u2248\u202f30\u202fs total** | \u2013 | Real\u2011world API latency adds ~0.2\u202fs per request \u2192 ~40\u202fs overall. |\n| **Similarity search (FAISS)** | 10\u202f000\u202fqueries\u202f/\u202fs on 1\u202fCPU core (sub\u2011ms per query) | 0.8\u202fms (p99) | IVF\u2011PQ + HNSW refinement gives <1\u202fms latency for 50\u202fk vectors. |\n| **LLM generation** (GPT\u20114o) | 60\u202ftokens\u202f/\u202fs per request (\u2248\u202f0.5\u202fs for 300\u2011token answer) | 500\u202fms (p99) | Dependent on prompt length; cost dominates, not latency. |\n| **End\u2011to\u2011end RAG (embedding\u2011search\u2011generate)** | **\u2248\u202f1\u202freq\u202f/\u202fsecond** (including LLM call) under 1\u202fs total | 900\u202fms (p99) | Sufficient for internal support bots; can be scaled horizontally. |\n\n### Load\u2011Testing Scenarios  \n\n| Test | Load | Expected metrics |\n|------|------|-------------------|\n| **Baseline** | 1\u202freq\u202f/\u202fs | End\u2011to\u2011end latency\u202f\u2248\u202f0.7\u202fs; CPU\u202f\u2248\u202f15\u202f% |\n| **Moderate** | 10\u202freq\u202f/\u202fs (spike) | Latency\u202f\u2248\u202f1.2\u202fs; CPU\u202f\u2248\u202f45\u202f% (search still <\u202f5\u202f%); LLM API dominates cost, not compute |\n| **Stress** | 50\u202freq\u202f/\u202fs (burst) | Latency\u202f\u2248\u202f2.5\u202fs; queueing on LLM API; need horizontal autoscaling of the orchestration layer (K8s pods) |\n| **Sustained high\u2011load** | 20\u202freq\u202f/\u202fs continuous | Add 2\u20113 additional worker pods; cost scales linearly with LLM usage |\n\n> **Recommendation:** Deploy the orchestration (FastAPI/Flask) behind an autoscaling Kubernetes HPA that adds a pod when CPU\u202f>\u202f70\u202f% or request latency\u202f>\u202f1\u202fs. The vector store can stay on a single node; replication is optional for HA.\n\n---\n\n## 4.  Cost\u2011Per\u2011Prediction (One RAG query)\n\n| Cost Item | Calculation | Cost |\n|-----------|-------------|------|\n| **Embedding lookup** (vector similarity) | Negligible (CPU <\u202f$0.001 per 1\u202f000 queries) | **\u2248\u202f$0.0001** |\n| **LLM generation** (GPT\u20114o, 300\u202ftokens) | 300\u202f/\u202f1\u202f000\u202f\u00d7\u202f$0.005 = $0.0015 | **\u2248\u202f$0.0015** |\n| **API overhead (embedding call for query)** | 350\u202ftokens\u202f\u00d7\u202f$0.0004\u202f/\u202f1\u202fk = $0.00014 | **\u2248\u202f$0.0002** |\n| **Total per request** | \u2013 | **\u2248\u202f$0.0018** (\u2248\u202f0.18\u202f\u00a2)** |\n\n> **Annualised cost** for 1\u202fM queries \u2248 **$1,800** (plus storage & compute).  \n\n---\n\n## 5.  Cost\u2011Efficiency Recommendations  \n\n| Area | Option | Cost Impact | Why it\u2019s optimal |\n|------|--------|-------------|------------------|\n| **Embedding generation** | **Batch to `text\u2011embedding\u2011ada\u2011002`** (64\u2011doc batches) | Reduces per\u2011token cost by ~15\u202f% (fewer API round\u2011trips) | Same quality, lower request\u2011overhead. |\n| **Vector store** | **FAISS on\u2011prem** (single VM, 8\u202fGB RAM) | ~**$0** (except VM) vs. managed Pinecone (~$0.12\u202f/\u202fGB\u202f/\u202fmonth) | For 0.5\u202fGB index, FAISS costs \u2248\u202f$20/mo for a small VM vs. $60/mo Pinecone. |\n| **LLM generation** | **GPT\u20114\u2011Turbo** (if answer quality tolerates) | $0.003\u202f/\u202f1\u202fk\u202ftokens vs. $0.005 (\u2248\u202f40\u202f% cheaper) | Same latency, slightly lower creativity. |\n| **Autoscaling** | **K8s HPA** with CPU & latency metrics | Avoids over\u2011provisioning; only pay for active pods | Keeps monthly compute <\u202f$30 for a 2\u2011core pod. |\n| **Caching** | **Cache top\u2011N retrieval results** (Redis, 5\u2011minute TTL) | Cuts vector\u2011search CPU by ~30\u202f% for repeated queries | Beneficial for FAQs & hot topics. |\n| **Document chunking** | **Chunk size 300\u2011400\u202ftokens** (\u2248\u202f2\u202fKB) | Keeps number of vectors \u2248\u202f50\u202fk, avoids index blow\u2011up | Larger chunks reduce vector count but hurt relevance; this is a sweet\u2011spot. |\n\n### Rough Monthly Cost Estimate (AWS EC2\u2011t3.medium + Managed LLM)\n\n| Component | Monthly price (USD) |\n|-----------|--------------------|\n| **EC2 t3.medium (2\u202fvCPU, 4\u202fGB RAM)** \u2013 runs FAISS + API gateway | **$30** |\n| **Redis ElasticCache (cache layer, 0.5\u202fGB)** | **$10** |\n| **Embedding API (50\u202fk docs once + 1\u202fM queries)** | 50\u202fk\u202f\u00d7\u202f0.0002\u202f\u2248\u202f$10 (one\u2011time) + 1\u202fM\u202f\u00d7\u202f0.0002\u202f\u2248\u202f$200 |\n| **LLM generation (1\u202fM queries \u00d7 300\u202ftokens)** | 1\u202fM\u202f\u00d7\u202f$0.0015\u202f\u2248\u202f$1,500 |\n| **Total** | **\u2248\u202f$1,750 / month** |\n\n*If you switch to GPT\u20114\u2011Turbo the LLM line drops to \u2248\u202f$900, bringing the total to ~**$1,150 / month**.*\n\n---\n\n## 6.  Risks, Uncertainties & Mitigations  \n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|--------|------------|\n| **Embedding quality drift** (new docs differ in style) | Medium | Retrieval relevance \u2193 | Periodic re\u2011embedding (weekly) and monitoring of retrieval\u2011accuracy metrics. |\n| **API price changes** (OpenAI may raise token rates) | Medium | Cost \u2191 | Keep a self\u2011hosted embedding fallback (Sentence\u2011Transformers + GPU) for large batches. |\n| **Latency spikes due to LLM throttling** | Low\u2011Medium | SLA breach | Implement request queue + exponential back\u2011off; optionally pre\u2011warm a smaller \u201ccheap\u201d model for fallback. |\n| **Vector\u2011store scaling limits** (future growth >\u202f500\u202fk docs) | Low now | Need re\u2011architecture | Design the pipeline to allow migration to a managed service (Pinecone, Qdrant) without code changes (abstracted via a repository pattern). |\n| **Data privacy / compliance** | Low (internal) | Legal risk | Encrypt data at rest (EBS) and in transit; ensure LLM calls do not send PHI (strip sensitive fields). |\n\n---\n\n## 7.  Actionable, Prioritized Roadmap  \n\n| Priority | Step | Owner | Deliverable | Timeline |\n|----------|------|-------|-------------|----------|\n| **1\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Provision a modest VM (t3.medium) + Redis** | Infra | Running instance with FAISS index loaded | 1\u202fwk |\n| **2\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Batch\u2011embed 50\u202fk docs** (Ada\u2011002, 64\u2011doc batches) | Data Eng | `embeddings.parquet` + FAISS index (`.faiss`) | 2\u202fwks |\n| **3\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Implement API gateway** (FastAPI) exposing `/query` (embedding \u2192 search \u2192 LLM) | Backend | End\u2011to\u2011end RAG service (local) | 3\u202fwks |\n| **4\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Load\u2011test** using Locust or k6 (10, 20, 50\u202fRPS) \u2192 capture latency, CPU, cost | QA | Test report + autoscaling thresholds | 4\u202fwks |\n| **5\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Cost\u2011optimisation**: switch to GPT\u20114\u2011Turbo, enable caching, evaluate self\u2011hosted embeddings for >\u202f1\u202fM docs | Ops | Updated cost model + CI pipeline for re\u2011embedding | 5\u20116\u202fwks |\n| **6\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Monitoring & Alerting** (Prometheus + Grafana) for query latency, LLM error rates, storage usage | DevOps | Dashboard + alerts | 6\u202fwks |\n| **7\ufe0f\u20e3** | **Documentation & SOP** (how to add new docs, re\u2011index, scale) | Docs | Run\u2011book | 7\u202fwks |\n\n---\n\n## 8.  Summary (Bottom\u2011Line)\n\n| Metric | Value (for 50\u202fk docs) |\n|--------|----------------------|\n| **Total storage** | **\u2248\u202f0.4\u202fGB** (raw\u202f+\u202fvectors\u202f+\u202fmetadata) |\n| **Embedding time** | **\u2248\u202f30\u201145\u202fs** (single\u2011batch API) |\n| **Search latency** | **\u2264\u202f1\u202fms** (FAISS) |\n| **End\u2011to\u2011end query latency** | **\u2248\u202f0.7\u202fs** (typical) |\n| **Cost per query** | **\u2248\u202f$0.0018** (Ada\u2011002 + GPT\u20114o) |\n| **Monthly operating cost** | **$1.1\u202fk \u2013 $1.8\u202fk** (depends on LLM model) |\n| **Scalable to** | **\u2265\u202f500\u202fk docs** with <\u202f2\u202fGB storage; vector\u2011store remains sub\u2011second. |\n\n**Recommendation:** Deploy the RAG pipeline on a small, auto\u2011scaled compute node with a local FAISS index, use batch calls to `text\u2011embedding\u2011ada\u2011002`, and generate answers with GPT\u20114\u2011Turbo (or GPT\u20114o if higher quality is required). This configuration delivers sub\u2011second latency, keeps monthly spend under **$2\u202fk**, and leaves ample headroom for future growth or more aggressive caching strategies."
  }
}
